    "extracted text": "The paper studies 354 aluminum cast alloys with additions of Zr and Ni and their effects on high temperature tensile properties. The alloys were tested in both as-cast (AC) and T6 heat treated conditions. The T6 heat treatment involved solution heat treating at 495°C for 8h, quenched in warm water at 60°C, followed by artificial aging at 190°C for 2h. High temperature tensile tests were conducted at various temperatures from 25°C to 300°C. The results showed that tensile strength decreases with increasing temperature. Combined addition of 0.2wt% Zr and 0.2wt% Ni (alloy E) led to a 30% increase in tensile properties at 300°C compared to the base alloy.",
    "property mapping": "AA: 354 (mentioned in the text)\nTemper: AC (as-cast) and T6 (solution heat treated at 495°C for 8h, quenched at 60°C, and artificially aged at 190°C for 2h)\nUTS [MPa]: Ultimate tensile strength values in Tables 2\nYS [MPa]: Yield strength values in Tables 3\nTesting Temperatures: 25°C, 190°C, 250°C, and 300°C",
